{"type":"message","id":"076b762e","parentId":"191f7ec8","timestamp":"2026-02-26T08:57:26.221Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_function_xf0e4z8soc7c_1","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"🦞 OpenClaw 2026.2.24 (df9a474) — Welcome to the command line: where dreams compile and confidence segfaults.\n\nUsage: openclaw agents [options] [command]\n\nManage isolated agents (workspaces + auth + routing)\n\nOptions:\n  -h, --help    Display help for command\n\nCommands:\n  add           Add a new isolated agent\n  delete        Delete an agent and prune workspace/state\n  list          List configured agents\n  set-identity  Update an agent identity (name/theme/emoji/avatar)\n\nDocs: https://docs.openclaw.ai/cli/agents"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":1507,"aggregated":"🦞 OpenClaw 2026.2.24 (df9a474) — Welcome to the command line: where dreams compile and confidence segfaults.\n\nUsage: openclaw agents [options] [command]\n\nManage isolated agents (workspaces + auth + routing)\n\nOptions:\n  -h, --help    Display help for command\n\nCommands:\n  add           Add a new isolated agent\n  delete        Delete an agent and prune workspace/state\n  list          List configured agents\n  set-identity  Update an agent identity (name/theme/emoji/avatar)\n\nDocs: https://docs.openclaw.ai/cli/agents","cwd":"/home/one/.openclaw/agents/leader-agent"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1772096246218}}
{"type":"message","id":"6c29a3c0","parentId":"076b762e","timestamp":"2026-02-26T08:57:30.048Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me check \"agent\" command to see if I can invoke an agent turn.","thinkingSignature":"102951de5de744b303645d7102f514897c964e76baa6884cd1c9876042acdf1c"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_pkd33s75elma_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"openclaw agent --help 2>&1"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.5","usage":{"input":5613,"output":51,"cacheRead":7322,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":12986,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1772096246221}}
{"type":"message","id":"d561ff91","parentId":"6c29a3c0","timestamp":"2026-02-26T08:57:31.542Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_function_pkd33s75elma_1","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"🦞 OpenClaw 2026.2.24 (df9a474) — Meta wishes they shipped this fast.\n\nUsage: openclaw agent [options]\n\nRun an agent turn via the Gateway (use --local for embedded)\n\nOptions:\n  --agent <id>               Agent id (overrides routing bindings)\n  --channel <channel>        Delivery channel:\n                             last|telegram|whatsapp|discord|irc|googlechat|slack|signal|imessage|feishu|nostr|msteams|mattermost|nextcloud-talk|matrix|bluebubbles|line|zalo|zalouser|synology-chat|tlon\n                             (omit to use the main session channel)\n  --deliver                  Send the agent's reply back to the selected channel\n                             (default: false)\n  -h, --help                 Display help for command\n  --json                     Output result as JSON (default: false)\n  --local                    Run the embedded agent locally (requires model\n                             provider API keys in your shell) (default: false)\n  -m, --message <text>       Message body for the agent\n  --reply-account <id>       Delivery account id override\n  --reply-channel <channel>  Delivery channel override (separate from routing)\n  --reply-to <target>        Delivery target override (separate from session\n                             routing)\n  --session-id <id>          Use an explicit session id\n  -t, --to <number>          Recipient number in E.164 used to derive the\n                             session key\n  --thinking <level>         Thinking level: off | minimal | low | medium | high\n  --timeout <seconds>        Override agent command timeout (seconds, default\n                             600 or config value)\n  --verbose <on|off>         Persist agent verbose level for the session\n\nExamples:\n  openclaw agent --to +15555550123 --message \"status update\"\n    Start a new session.\n  openclaw agent --agent ops --message \"Summarize logs\"\n    Use a specific agent.\n  openclaw agent --session-id 1234 --message \"Summarize inbox\" --thinking medium\n    Target a session with explicit thinking level.\n  openclaw agent --to +15555550123 --message \"Trace logs\" --verbose on --json\n    Enable verbose logging and JSON output.\n  openclaw agent --to +15555550123 --message \"Summon reply\" --deliver\n    Deliver reply.\n  openclaw agent --agent ops --message \"Generate report\" --deliver --reply-channel slack --reply-to \"#reports\"\n    Send reply to a different channel/target.\n\nDocs: https://docs.openclaw.ai/cli/agent"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":1487,"aggregated":"🦞 OpenClaw 2026.2.24 (df9a474) — Meta wishes they shipped this fast.\n\nUsage: openclaw agent [options]\n\nRun an agent turn via the Gateway (use --local for embedded)\n\nOptions:\n  --agent <id>               Agent id (overrides routing bindings)\n  --channel <channel>        Delivery channel:\n                             last|telegram|whatsapp|discord|irc|googlechat|slack|signal|imessage|feishu|nostr|msteams|mattermost|nextcloud-talk|matrix|bluebubbles|line|zalo|zalouser|synology-chat|tlon\n                             (omit to use the main session channel)\n  --deliver                  Send the agent's reply back to the selected channel\n                             (default: false)\n  -h, --help                 Display help for command\n  --json                     Output result as JSON (default: false)\n  --local                    Run the embedded agent locally (requires model\n                             provider API keys in your shell) (default: false)\n  -m, --message <text>       Message body for the agent\n  --reply-account <id>       Delivery account id override\n  --reply-channel <channel>  Delivery channel override (separate from routing)\n  --reply-to <target>        Delivery target override (separate from session\n                             routing)\n  --session-id <id>          Use an explicit session id\n  -t, --to <number>          Recipient number in E.164 used to derive the\n                             session key\n  --thinking <level>         Thinking level: off | minimal | low | medium | high\n  --timeout <seconds>        Override agent command timeout (seconds, default\n                             600 or config value)\n  --verbose <on|off>         Persist agent verbose level for the session\n\nExamples:\n  openclaw agent --to +15555550123 --message \"status update\"\n    Start a new session.\n  openclaw agent --agent ops --message \"Summarize logs\"\n    Use a specific agent.\n  openclaw agent --session-id 1234 --message \"Summarize inbox\" --thinking medium\n    Target a session with explicit thinking level.\n  openclaw agent --to +15555550123 --message \"Trace logs\" --verbose on --json\n    Enable verbose logging and JSON output.\n  openclaw agent --to +15555550123 --message \"Summon reply\" --deliver\n    Deliver reply.\n  openclaw agent --agent ops --message \"Generate report\" --deliver --reply-channel slack --reply-to \"#reports\"\n    Send reply to a different channel/target.\n\nDocs: https://docs.openclaw.ai/cli/agent","cwd":"/home/one/.openclaw/agents/leader-agent"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1772096251539}}
{"type":"message","id":"257cfedf","parentId":"d561ff91","timestamp":"2026-02-26T08:57:38.041Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"我找到了如何与特定 agent 交互的方法！使用 `--agent` 参数可以定位到特定的 agent。让我尝试调用 design-agent 来进行设计。","thinkingSignature":"326b28d5fd3c91c19ae8781d14925f36a819ab9ad6f7d83b5f92de1ccc27ba63"},{"type":"text","text":"找到了！现在让我依次调用各个 agent：\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_w1w9njivoyyg_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"openclaw agent --agent design-agent --message \"## 任务：To-Do Web 前端设计\n\n**项目背景：**\n- 现有 REST API 端点：\n  - GET /todos - 获取所有待办\n  - GET /todos/{id} - 获取单个待办\n  - POST /todos - 创建待办（body: {\\\"title\\\": \\\"...\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"...\\\"}）\n  - PUT /todos/{id} - 更新待办（body: {\\\"title\\\": \\\"...\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"...\\\", \\\"completed\\\": true/false}）\n  - DELETE /todos/{id} - 删除待办\n- 技术栈后端：FastAPI + SQLite + SQLAlchemy\n\n**任务：**\n1. 设计一个简单的 Web 前端页面\n2. 功能：展示待办列表、添加、编辑（完成状态、修改内容）、删除\n3. 请提供：\n   - 页面结构\n   - 技术选型建议（纯HTML/JS或轻量框架）\n   - 前后端交互方式\n   - 简单的设计文档\n\n请直接输出设计文档内容。\" --timeout 120","timeout":180}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.5","usage":{"input":6239,"output":312,"cacheRead":7322,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":13873,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1772096251542}}
